# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 19 — Future Expansion

---

# Purpose

This section explicitly defines what DigiSwasthya anticipates but does **not** currently support.

Future expansion must extend the current product foundation.

It must not redefine existing entities, break state machines, or invalidate core business rules.

Anything listed here is out of current scope unless a future PDD revision moves it into supported capabilities.

---

# Expansion Principles

1. Core meanings of Order, Invoice, Payment, Return, Credit Note remain stable.
2. New participants (warehouses, manufacturers, transporters) become new entities/roles, not hacks on Pharmacy/Stockist.
3. Multiplicity (multi-branch, multi-warehouse) extends ownership/location models rather than duplicating businesses casually.
4. Integrations must obey Permissions, State Machines, and Calculations.
5. No future feature may require negative inventory or mutable issued financial history.

---

# 1. Multi-Branch Pharmacies

## Anticipated

- One pharmacy business with multiple retail branches
- Branch-level delivery addresses, receipt, and inventory
- Branch-level ordering preferences

## Not Current

- Single business = single operational location model remains default
- No first-class Branch entity yet

## Extension Rule

Branch should become a child of Business, not a second Business pretending to be a branch.

---

# 2. Multi-Warehouse Stockists

## Anticipated

- Multiple warehouses / godowns
- Warehouse-specific inventory and batches
- Dispatch from selected warehouse
- Inter-warehouse transfer

## Not Current

- Single inventory pool per stockist business

## Extension Rule

Inventory and Batch gain Location/Warehouse ownership; Order fulfilment gains source warehouse.

---

# 3. Manufacturers

## Anticipated

- Manufacturer onboarding
- Manufacturer → Stockist supply relationships
- Manufacturer catalogues / PTB feeds
- Batch genealogy from manufacturer

## Not Current

- Only Pharmacy ↔ Stockist trade

## Extension Rule

Manufacturer is a new business type/participant, not overloaded Stockist.

---

# 4. Inter-Stockist Transfers

## Anticipated

- Stockist-to-stockist stock movement
- Transfer orders, in-transit states, receiving confirmation

## Not Current

- No transfer order entity

## Extension Rule

Do not misuse Pharmacy Order/Return flows to simulate transfers.

---

# 5. Purchase Orders (Formal Procurement Documents)

## Anticipated

- Distinct Purchase Order document separate from fulfilment Order semantics if needed
- PO approvals, budgets, blanket POs

## Not Current

- Pharmacy “Order” is the purchase request used for trade

## Extension Rule

If PO is introduced, map clearly to existing Order/Invoice chain without dual conflicting truths.

---

# 6. Advanced Partial Fulfilment Policies

## Anticipated

- Rich backorder management
- Auto-split orders by availability
- Promised date commitments per line

## Current

- Partial fulfilment conceptually allowed; deep backorder suite not fully productized

---

# 7. Payment Gateway Automation

## Anticipated

- Online collection
- Auto-reconciliation references
- Instant payment confirmation webhooks

## Not Current

- Manual payment submission + stockist approval model

## Extension Rule

Gateway confirmation still creates Payment through official states; cannot bypass approval/audit requirements where business policy needs them.

---

# 8. Accounting Software Integrations

## Anticipated

- Tally/Zoho/others export or sync
- Chart of accounts mapping
- GST filing assistance exports

## Not Current

- In-platform financial documents only

## Extension Rule

External systems are projections; DigiSwasthya invoices/payments remain authoritative for platform trade disputes unless explicitly redefined.

---

# 9. Logistics Partner Integrations

## Anticipated

- Third-party transporters
- AWB numbers
- Live shipment tracking providers

## Not Current

- First-party Delivery entity and delivery staff model

## Extension Rule

External tracking updates Delivery states through allowed transitions only.

---

# 10. ABDM / Health Network Integration

## Anticipated

- ABHA-related identity hooks where relevant
- Regulated health network interoperability

## Not Current

- Pure B2B pharma commerce/operations; no clinical patient graph

## Extension Rule

Do not expand into EMR/patient management accidentally under ABDM work.

---

# 11. AI Ordering / Recommendations

## Anticipated

- Suggested reorder quantities
- Demand prediction
- Supplier recommendations
- Anomaly detection on payments/orders

## Not Current

- Manual ordering and operational queues

## Extension Rule

AI suggestions are advisory unless a user explicitly confirms; Accuracy Over Automation remains binding.

---

# 12. Credit Limits & Trade Finance

## Anticipated

- Formal credit limits per connection
- Temporary credit holds
- Financing partners

## Current

- Outstanding tracking exists; full credit-limit enforcement is optional/future-ready in calculations

---

# 13. Promotions, Schemes & Complex Pricing

## Anticipated

- Scheme packs (buy X get Y)
- Time-bound offers
- Slab pricing
- Customer group pricing matrices

## Current

- Base price, discounts, optional customer-specific terms conceptually

## Extension Rule

Pricing engine outputs must still snapshot onto order/invoice lines immutably.

---

# 14. Cold Chain / Special Handling

## Anticipated

- Temperature capture
- Special handling flags with enforcement
- Specialized delivery workflows

## Not Current

- Notes/storage conditions may exist informationally without full cold-chain compliance engine

---

# 15. Advanced Compliance Module

## Anticipated

- License expiry automation
- Schedule H/H1 controls beyond basic flags
- Mandatory reporting packs
- Recall orchestration across delivered customers

## Current

- Verification, expiry blocking, recall batch status basics

---

# 16. Marketplace Mode

## Anticipated

- Open discovery with escrow-like protections
- Platform commercial terms

## Not Current / Out of Scope Now

- Relationship/connection-based B2B trade among verified businesses
- Not a public consumer marketplace

---

# 17. Patient / Doctor / Rx Workflows

## Explicitly out of current product and not near-term expansion of this B2B core

- Patient management
- Doctor management
- e-prescriptions as clinical system
- Insurance claims as core
- Hospital ERP
- Lab management
- Consumer medicine delivery marketplace

These remain out of scope unless product strategy formally changes.

---

# 18. Multi-Currency / Cross-Border Trade

## Anticipated

- Multi-currency contracts
- FX handling

## Not Current

- INR-centric B2B domestic operations assumption

---

# 19. Business Merge / Split Tools

## Anticipated

- Governed merge of businesses
- Split branch carve-outs with history rules

## Not Current

- Manual/admin exceptional handling only; no self-serve merge

---

# 20. Subscription / SaaS Commercial Layer

## Anticipated

- Platform billing plans for businesses
- Feature entitlements by plan

## Not Current

- Product definition focuses on trade operations, not SaaS packaging

---

# Impact on Existing Documents

When a future item is adopted:

1. Update Product Foundation scope
2. Add/extend Entities + Entity Specifications
3. Extend Relationships & Rules
4. Add Capabilities + Capability Specs
5. Add Journeys
6. Extend State Machines
7. Add Calculations
8. Extend Permissions
9. Add Notifications
10. Add Search/Dashboard entries
11. Add Edge Cases + Error Behaviour
12. Add Acceptance Criteria
13. Update Glossary

No feature skips this sequence.

---

# Completion Criteria

Current vs future boundaries are explicit enough that engineering/design cannot accidentally invent unsupported future domains as if they were present.

